{
    "description": "Scope fork/revert and effect-stream observation benchmark procedure for pnpm bench:scopes and pnpm check:scopes. The benchmark section is digested into every result artifact; the slo section is not, so budgets can change without re-measuring. Dimensions mirror Section 4 and Appendix C of arXiv 2605.10913 v3 (world sizes, a 5+3 mutation pattern at K=4, a per-write size sweep, per-event record and observe overhead through 200 steps) at sizes that fit a developer machine; no number from the paper is used.",
    "benchmark": {
        "branching": {
            "baselineWrites": 5,
            "branchCount": 4,
            "branchWrites": 1,
            "defaultWriteBytes": 10240,
            "repetitions": 3
        },
        "fork": {
            "repetitions": 10,
            "warmupIterations": 2
        },
        "mutationSweep": {
            "world": "medium",
            "writeBytes": [1024, 10240, 1048576, 10485760]
        },
        "naming": {
            "claimPrefix": "claim:bench:",
            "commandPrefix": "bench:scope:",
            "effectKind": "bench.scope.event",
            "handlerId": "handler:bench.scope.event",
            "logicalTimeMilliseconds": 1000,
            "programId": "bench:scope-observation.v1",
            "sourceBinding": "source"
        },
        "observation": {
            "observerCounts": [0, 1, 4],
            "sessionRepetitions": 3,
            "steps": [1, 10, 50, 100, 200]
        },
        "resultDirectory": "docs/generated/benchmarks",
        "resultFormat": "shepherd.scope-benchmark",
        "resultFormatVersion": 1,
        "resultPrefix": "scope-benchmark-",
        "storage": {
            "flushCommand": ["sync"],
            "settleAttempts": 50,
            "settleDelayMilliseconds": 100,
            "settleToleranceBytes": 65536
        },
        "temporaryDirectoryPrefix": "shepherd-scope-bench-",
        "worlds": [
            {
                "fileBytes": 3072,
                "files": 10,
                "id": "small"
            },
            {
                "fileBytes": 102400,
                "files": 100,
                "id": "medium"
            },
            {
                "fileBytes": 1048576,
                "files": 100,
                "id": "large"
            }
        ]
    },
    "slo": {
        "budgetPolicy": "Each host class's budgets come from three pnpm bench:scopes runs on that class's measurement host, the last of which is the committed result artifact: every budget bounds p95 at three times the worst measured p95 of the three runs, rounded up to two significant figures. Budgeted metrics are fork_ms and revert_ms for every measured backend and world, and record_ms and observe_ms at the largest configured step count. The threefold headroom absorbs run-to-run noise and a loaded machine; it is not a claim about any other host. macos-arm64-apfs: set on 2026-09-25 on the reference host (Apple M4 Pro, 14 cores, 48 GiB, Darwin 27.0.0, APFS, Node 24.17.0, SQLite 3.53.0; copy and clone conformant). linux-arm64-xfs-privileged-container: set on 2026-09-25 from three pnpm bench:scopes:linux runs as root in a privileged node:24-bookworm container (Node 24.21.0, SQLite 3.53.4) in OrbStack's Linux VM (kernel 7.0.14-orbstack, 14 CPUs, 16 GiB) on the same reference host, temporary directory on a loopback XFS reflink=1 image on tmpfs; copy, clone, and overlay conformant.",
        "hostClasses": [
            {
                "budgets": {
                    "fork_ms/clone/large": {
                        "max": 4400,
                        "statistic": "p95"
                    },
                    "fork_ms/clone/medium": {
